# Severity and seams

Hard stops when editing core triage modules:

- `rankSeverity` stays pure and rule-based. Never let Workers AI choose or override P0–P3.
- Signal escalation is at most **one** level; keep thresholds as named constants.
- `investigateCodebase` remains a DI seam (`InvestigationDependencies`); do not hard-wire Octokit into the agent loop.
- Webhook handler: verify HMAC on the raw body; ack fast with `ctx.waitUntil` — never await triage/AI/GitHub/Slack/D1 on the request path.
- Sentry signal fetch: degrade to `null` / base severity on missing token, rate limit, or HTTP failure — never throw into the webhook path.
- Auto-remediation: P0/P1 must not auto-fix; return `null` when a patch cannot be localized confidently.
- Slack, PagerDuty, D1, and GitHub remediations are adapters via explicit dependencies — not core decision logic.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — LLM picks priority
severity = await ai.run(...); // "reply with P0-P3"

// ✅ GOOD — deterministic tool, AI only writes report text
const severity = rankSeverity({ level, project, culprit, signals });
const reportText = await synthesizeReport(payload, ai, severity, investigation);
```

Prefer Accepted ADRs (`docs/adr/`) over inventing new priority or routing heuristics.
